         frame, data, target = _convert_data_dataframe(\n 990 |             \"load_diabetes\", data, target, feature_names, target_columns\n 991 |         )\n 992 | \n 993 |     if return_X_y:\n 994 |         return data, target\n 995 | \n 996 |     return Bunch(\n 997 |         data=data,\n 998 |         target=target,\n 999 |         frame=frame,\n1000 |         DESCR=fdescr,\n1001 |         feature_names=feature_names,\n1002 |         data_filename=data_filename,\n1003 |         target_filename=target_filename,\n1004 |         data_module=DATA_MODULE,\n1005 |     )\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/calibration.py`.\nFound file `examples/calibration/plot_calibration.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let me examine the calibration plotting functionality more closely:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sklearn/calibration.py:CalibrationDisplay']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/calibration.py:CalibrationDisplay`...\n### Search Result:\nInvalid name. \nHint: Valid entity name should be formatted as \"file_path:QualifiedName\" or just \"file_path\".\n"}, {"content": "Let me try searching for the display classes and methods:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['CalibrationDisplay', 'plot']</parameter>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>sklearn/calibration.py</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"CalibrationDisplay\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/calibration.py:_sigmoid_calibration`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n722 | 