mns.\n3757 | \n3758 |     Returns\n3759 |     -------\n3760 |     nd.array\n3761 |         The concatenation of list_of_columns with sep.\n3762 |     \"\"\"\n3763 |     try:\n3764 |         result = cat_core(list_of_columns, sep)\n3765 |     except TypeError:\n3766 |         # if there are any non-string values (wrong dtype or hidden behind\n3767 |         # object dtype), np.sum will fail; catch and return with better message\n3768 |         for column in list_of_columns:\n3769 |             dtype = lib.infer_dtype(column, skipna=True)\n3770 |             if dtype not in [\"string\", \"empty\"]:\n3771 |                 raise TypeError(\n3772 |                     \"Concatenation requires list-likes containing only \"\n3773 |                     \"strings (or missing values). Offending values found in \"\n3774 |                     f\"column {dtype}\"\n3775 |                 ) from None\n3776 |     return result\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me get the specific content of the key file mentioned:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:StringMethods._validate`.\n```\n221 | def _validate(data):\n222 |         \"\"\"\n223 |         Auxiliary function for StringMethods, infers and checks dtype of data.\n224 | \n225 |         This is a \"first line of defence\" at the creation of the StringMethods-\n226 |         object, and just checks that the dtype is in the\n227 |         *union* of the allowed types over all string methods below; this\n228 |         restriction 